          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The earlier result proves one finite comparison, but its error bound becomes nonuniform as the coefficient index grows. I’m examining two structural issues in parallel: what quantitative information can survive an order-induction step, and whether the chosen reference can support positivity at arbitrarily large orders.\n"
