          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "I found a stronger obstruction than the handoff recorded: the existing complete error payment eventually exceeds its reference margin at every fixed order. That failure persists after all polynomial cancellations are collected. The actual omitted theta coefficients, however, become relatively smaller at large indices, so the obstruction is to this error payment, not to theta positivity. I’m working out that distinction and checking what it leaves available for continuation.\n"
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
