              "Completed the bounded B03 investigation and one full-source repair attempt.\n\n- [Note07](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/07_positive_theta_primitives/01_jensen/01_mellin_curvature/10_radial_green_determinants/notes/07_RGD_B03_R2_EXACT_PAYMENT_OBSTRUCTION_AND_TRUE_TAIL_20261104.md) proves that the **existing complete error payment eventually fails at every fixed order**, although the actual omitted coefficient tail decays.\n- [Note08](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/07_positive_theta_primitives/01_jensen/01_mellin_curvature/10_radial_green_determinants/notes/08_RGD_B02_R1_COMPLETE_SOURCE_CONTOUR_MARGIN_20261104.md) develops a **conditional complete-source mechanism** with explicit \\(k\\gtrsim r^8\\) dependence and all exterior errors paid. Its canonical scalar estimates remain open.\n\nA preprint already reports a stronger cubic tail region, so the eighth-power route is retained as a comparison tool. Its proof remains unaudited here. [Primary source](https://arxiv.org/html/2607.16795v1)\n\nThe central unresolved region is **fixed small \\(k\\) and \\(k\\) comparable with \\(r\\)**. No all-order positivity theorem was obtained.\n\nProgress and chat history are recorded. The [continuation and model-change guide](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/07_positive_theta_primitives/01_jensen/01_mellin_curvature/10_radial_green_determinants/research-progress/handoffs/11_RGD_B03_B02_RETURN_AND_MODEL_CONTINUATION_20261104.md) recommends **[E] RGD-E04 r4 — Sol** for assessment, then **[B] RGD-B02 r2 — Astra** for that missing region."
