              "Completed **RGD-B02 r2** as a bounded research return.\n\n- **Fixed index:** derived an explicit order induction using reciprocal determinant duality. The relative error contracts geometrically; a coarse canonical initialization gives \\(D_{r,1}>0\\) for \\(r\\ge1500\\), using published finite-zero inputs.\n- **Growing index:** proved exact failure of every fixed finite-pole reference, including boundary cases. The chosen error bound also fails when index grows proportionally to order.\n- The mechanism has [direct prior art](https://kenan.works/posts/fifteen-shifts-of-xi/). No new positivity range or all-index theorem is claimed.\n\nSaved the [research note](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/07_positive_theta_primitives/01_jensen/01_mellin_curvature/10_radial_green_determinants/notes/10_RGD_B02_R2_RECIPROCAL_POLE_INDUCTION_AND_SCOPED_STOP_20261104.md), checks and references; updated progress and chat history.\n\n**Next: [E] RGD-E04 r5 — Sol**, a bounded analytical assessment. The [continuation and model-change guide](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/07_positive_theta_primitives/01_jensen/01_mellin_curvature/10_radial_green_determinants/research-progress/handoffs/14_RGD_B02_R2_RETURN_AND_MODEL_CONTINUATION_20261104.md) explains what a subsequent mechanism must overcome: maintaining a positive reference margin as dimension grows while controlling the complete signed residual."
